Category: IT Services

Location: Fort Colombo Sri Lanka

We are urgently looking for a REMOTE Senior Test Automation Specialist with +5 years of test experience with complex web application platforms for an international organization in New York. Candidates must have hands-on experience working with Angular, Node.js, MongoDB in teams building large consumer-facing web applications from the ground up.

Candidates need to be fluent in English. All positions are long-term. This position is open for freelancers and employees.

Candidates need to be able to work +5 hours per day in the normal office hours of New York, US. (Example 9 AM NY time equals 7:30 PM.)

Tasks and deliverables:

• Work within an agile team to ensure the quality of complex MEAN applications;

• Develop, modify, and execute functional test scripts and analyze bugs for systems in development;

• Work closely with developers to recognize the potential for any operational issues, assess risks, and resolve issues proactively;

• Create test automation frameworks from the ground up using Selenium WebDriver;

• Automate API testing using Postman and similar tools;

• Perform load testing using a variety of tools as per industry standards and suggest solutions for performance issues;

• Perform penetration testing and another security-related testing as needed;

• Record defect details and create reports outlining the types of defects found and the steps taken to resolve them and update the regression test framework;

• Maintain knowledgebase documentation in SharePoint ;

Profile:

• Bachelor or Master degree;

• +5 years of experience in Quality Assurance for complex web application platforms;

• Experience designing, developing, managing, and executing test cases, preferably using QA management tools;

• Proven experience with test automation using Selenium and the ability to write scripts and perform API testing;

• Experience with security testing, integration testing, end-to-end testing, and load testing;

• Mobile application testing, browser compatibility, and accessibility testing experience;

• Experience in identifying, analyzing, documenting, and reporting test results;

• Experience with GitLab and CI/CD pipelines;

• Good interpersonal skills to work with developers in an agile environment;

• Experience in MS Teams and SharePoint documentation is a plus;

• Fluent in English;

Offered:

• A challenging role for an international organization in New York;

• Attractive salary package;

